1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,764
She pulled the trigger on her own son.

2
00:00:02,814 --> 00:00:03,744
Both barrels.

3
00:00:03,794 --> 00:00:04,669
Silver.

4
00:00:04,719 --> 00:00:06,167
Nothing happened.

5
00:00:06,637 --> 00:00:07,587
I'm a werewolf.

6
00:00:07,637 --> 00:00:09,062
So's her son,

7
00:00:09,112 --> 00:00:09,782
Danny.

8
00:00:09,832 --> 00:00:10,517
My best mate.

9
00:00:10,567 --> 00:00:12,132
Since his uncle Mick died,

10
00:00:12,182 --> 00:00:14,395
she's kept the watch on our street.

11
00:00:14,625 --> 00:00:16,005
Danny ran for the moor.

12
00:00:16,055 --> 00:00:17,787
She didn't go after him.

13
00:00:17,857 --> 00:00:19,634
She broke the gun open.

14
00:00:19,684 --> 00:00:21,669
Both barrels were empty.

15
00:00:21,819 --> 00:00:23,084
She'd never loaded it.

16
00:00:23,134 --> 00:00:24,260
Not once.

17
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:27,391
Then she gave me a page from Mick's notebook.

18
00:00:27,441 --> 00:00:27,886
August,

19
00:00:27,936 --> 00:00:29,276
two thousand and six.

20
00:00:29,326 --> 00:00:30,496
His left hand,

21
00:00:30,546 --> 00:00:31,460
shaking.

22
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:32,510
D. bit the boy.

23
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:33,260
Got him off.

24
00:00:33,310 --> 00:00:34,774
Cost me the arm.

25
00:00:35,164 --> 00:00:36,084
I was the boy.

26
00:00:36,134 --> 00:00:37,301
I was eight.

27
00:00:37,771 --> 00:00:40,117
Mick didn't lose his arm to a wolf.

28
00:00:40,167 --> 00:00:42,229
He lost it pulling one off me.

29
00:00:42,859 --> 00:00:43,474
By dawn,

30
00:00:43,524 --> 00:00:45,395
my hands were mine again.

31
00:00:45,464 --> 00:00:47,506
But Danny never came home.

32
00:00:47,656 --> 00:00:48,666
From my window,

33
00:00:48,716 --> 00:00:50,861
I saw him at the edge of the moor.

34
00:00:50,911 --> 00:00:51,646
Two eyes.

35
00:00:51,696 --> 00:00:52,676
And beside them,

36
00:00:52,726 --> 00:00:54,105
a smaller pair.

37
00:00:54,255 --> 00:00:55,342
Come out.
